<main id="main">

<section class="tl-hero"><div class="tl-w tl-hero-g"><div class="tl-hero-t"><p class="tl-k">An independent tailoring journal</p><h1>Every great suit<br>begins with<br><em>a tape measure.</em></h1><p class="tl-sig tl-hero-s">fit is everything</p><p class="tl-lead">Tailors explains the craft behind a well-cut suit: how to measure yourself, how bespoke differs from made-to-measure, and which cloth suits your seasons. Two free tools help you start.</p>
<div class="tl-hero-a"><a class="tl-btn" href="#size">Find your jacket size</a><a class="tl-lnk" href="#cloth">Choose a cloth &rarr;</a></div></div>
<div class="tl-hero-v"><figure class="tl-pc tl-pc1"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1788009732092-59a1eea5daa1?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=640&q=75" alt="tailoring scissors and a measuring tape on white fabric" width="560" height="640" fetchpriority="high"></figure><figure class="tl-pc tl-pc2"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1515736076039-a3ca66043b27?auto=format&fit=crop&w=300&h=380&q=75" alt="a man in a grey notched-lapel suit jacket" width="300" height="380" fetchpriority="high"></figure><svg class="tl-chalk" viewBox="0 0 200 200" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 180 C60 120 40 60 110 30 S190 60 180 120" /><path d="M150 150l20 20M170 150l-20 20"/></svg><p class="tl-tag"><span>No.</span>38R</p></div></div></section>

<section class="tl-s tl-sz" id="size"><div class="tl-w tl-sz-g"><div><p class="tl-k">Tool I</p><h2 class="rv">Jacket size finder</h2><p class="tl-p">Measure your chest at its fullest point and your waist where you wear your trousers, then add your height. We suggest a jacket size, length and the &ldquo;drop&rdquo; between chest and waist.</p>
<div class="tl-units" role="group" aria-label="Units"><button type="button" class="on" data-u="in">Inches</button><button type="button" data-u="cm">Centimetres</button></div>
<label class="tl-lb" for="sz-c">Chest <b id="sz-cv"></b></label><input type="range" id="sz-c" min="32" max="56" step=".5" value="40" class="tl-rng">
<label class="tl-lb" for="sz-w">Waist <b id="sz-wv"></b></label><input type="range" id="sz-w" min="26" max="52" step=".5" value="34" class="tl-rng">
<label class="tl-lb" for="sz-h">Height <b id="sz-hv"></b></label><input type="range" id="sz-h" min="60" max="78" value="70" class="tl-rng"></div>
<div class="tl-ticket" aria-live="polite"><div class="tl-ticket-h"><span>Fitting ticket</span><span>No. 0426</span></div><p class="tl-sig">your size</p><b id="sz-s">40R</b><dl><div><dt>US / UK</dt><dd id="sz-us"></dd></div><div><dt>EU</dt><dd id="sz-eu"></dd></div><div><dt>Drop</dt><dd id="sz-d"></dd></div><div><dt>Cut</dt><dd id="sz-cut"></dd></div></dl><p class="tl-note" id="sz-n"></p><figure class="tl-ticket-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1789993563952-13b119ac7a6a?auto=format&fit=crop&w=440&h=200&q=75" alt="a green measuring tape draped over black leather" width="440" height="200" loading="lazy"></figure></div></div></section>

<section class="tl-s tl-cl" id="cloth"><div class="tl-w"><div class="tl-cl-h"><div><p class="tl-k">Tool II</p><h2 class="rv">Cloth chooser</h2><p class="tl-p">The cloth matters as much as the cut. Tell us when and how you will wear the suit and we suggest a fabric, a weight and a weave.</p></div><figure class="tl-cl-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1681003564665-62848f8d481e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=620&h=260&q=75" alt="a shelf filled with folded fabrics in many colours" width="620" height="260" loading="lazy"></figure></div>
<div class="tl-cl-g"><div class="tl-qs"><p class="tl-lb">Season</p><div class="tl-chips" data-q="s"><button type="button" class="on" data-v="0">Spring / summer</button><button type="button" data-v="1">All year</button><button type="button" data-v="2">Autumn / winter</button></div>
<p class="tl-lb">Climate</p><div class="tl-chips" data-q="c"><button type="button" data-v="0">Hot &amp; humid</button><button type="button" class="on" data-v="1">Temperate</button><button type="button" data-v="2">Cold</button></div>
<p class="tl-lb">Occasion</p><div class="tl-chips" data-q="o"><button type="button" data-v="0">Office, often</button><button type="button" class="on" data-v="1">Weddings &amp; events</button><button type="button" data-v="2">Weekend, relaxed</button></div></div>
<div class="tl-sw" aria-live="polite"><div class="tl-sw-c" id="cl-sw"></div><div class="tl-sw-t"><p class="tl-sig" id="cl-k">the cloth</p><h3 id="cl-t"></h3><p id="cl-d"></p><ul class="tl-sw-l"><li><span>Weight</span><b id="cl-w"></b></li><li><span>Weave</span><b id="cl-v"></b></li><li><span>Colours</span><b id="cl-c"></b></li></ul></div></div></div></div></section>

<section class="tl-s tl-pr"><div class="tl-w"><div class="tl-pr-h"><p class="tl-k">In the workroom</p><h2 class="rv">From roll to rail, in four stages</h2></div><ol class="tl-steps"><li class="tl-st rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1765618779183-edb1806ab3e7?auto=format&fit=crop&w=360&h=440&q=75" alt="a close-up of a sewing machine needle" width="360" height="440" loading="lazy"></figure><span class="tl-st-n">01</span><b>Stitch</b><p>Seams are pressed open and stitched in stages, so the coat can still be adjusted.</p></li><li class="tl-st rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1586216583199-a2413508bb62?auto=format&fit=crop&w=360&h=440&q=75" alt="a hand holding a black thread spool and silver scissors" width="360" height="440" loading="lazy"></figure><span class="tl-st-n">02</span><b>Baste</b><p>A loose white tacking thread holds the first fitting together.</p></li><li class="tl-st rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1760815012005-d1dd61bf6cd2?auto=format&fit=crop&w=360&h=440&q=75" alt="a vintage sewing machine with fabric under the needle" width="360" height="440" loading="lazy"></figure><span class="tl-st-n">03</span><b>Sew</b><p>Long straight seams go to the machine; shaping work stays by hand.</p></li><li class="tl-st rv"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1681003258654-10f89d4e4753?auto=format&fit=crop&w=360&h=440&q=75" alt="a pile of thread spools in different colours" width="360" height="440" loading="lazy"></figure><span class="tl-st-n">04</span><b>Finish</b><p>Buttonholes, linings and the final press bring the coat to life.</p></li></ol></div></section>

<section class="tl-gd"><div class="tl-w tl-gd-g"><a class="tl-gc rv" href="bespoke-made-to-measure-guide.html"><span class="tl-gc-p">Pattern piece A</span><b>Bespoke vs Made-to-Measure vs Off-the-Rack</b><p>Three ways to buy a suit, and what you really pay for in each.</p></a><a class="tl-gc tl-gc2 rv" href="how-to-take-measurements-guide.html"><span class="tl-gc-p">Pattern piece B</span><b>How to Take Your Measurements</b><p>Chest, waist, seat, sleeve and inseam, measured like a tailor.</p></a></div></section>

</main>
